WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:04.220
Tywin Lannister: The Westerlands are all bounded
by three natural defenses.

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:07.950
Mountain, sea, and forest.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:12.720
Necessary barriers when the land is as rich
as ours.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:17.230
From our mines come the gold and silver that
fuel the rest of Westeros.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:23.680
From Lannisport, our largest city, come the
most skillful gold and silversmiths in the

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:24.680
land.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:28.200
Yet, geography alone is not strength.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.820
The Westerlands would have been sacked and
pillaged for thousands of years if it had

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.250
not been for the men who ruled it.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.890
My family.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.750
House Lannister.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:45.020
According to legend, we trace their descent
to Lann the Clever, a trickster of the Dawn

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:50.910
Age, who swindled the Casterlys out of Casterly
Rock, their ancient castle.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:54.170
A childish story, but not without merit.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:01:00.469
One, a mind can and should be a weapon in
a man's arsenal.

00:01:00.469 --> 00:01:05.639
Two, Lann must've been clever enough not to
rely solely on his wits.

00:01:05.639 --> 00:01:08.959
After all, where today is House Casterly?

00:01:08.959 --> 00:01:16.109
Three, by keeping the Casterly name on the
castle, Lann reminded the world of the price

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:18.630
of getting in his way.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:21.250
The Reynes ignored all these lessons.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.759
Not content with being the second-richest
family, they sought to challenge the first:

00:01:27.759 --> 00:01:29.039
mine.

00:01:29.039 --> 00:01:32.969
My father had put up with their insults and
disrespect.

00:01:32.969 --> 00:01:39.049
When I came of age, I led our army to teach
them what they should have known.

00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:45.630
Some people say I was too harsh, that eradicating
every member of their family was not necessary.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:52.369
But now there are no bannermen as loyal to
their lord as the Westerlands to us.

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:58.010
If any lord bridles at our authority, I have
only to send a singer with a harp, and he

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:00.219
falls back into line.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:04.709
Fools look at the Westerlands and see gold.

00:02:04.709 --> 00:02:08.729
Fools see our wealth and call it strength.

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:11.710
Gold is just another rock.

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:15.700
The Westerlands are strong because of House
Lannister.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.110
From strong leadership comes unity.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.470
From unity comes power.

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:25.690
Jaime Lannister:My ancestor, King Loren of
House Lannister, was head of the wealthiest

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:27.950
family in the Seven Kingdoms.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:32.420
When King Loren joined his forces to Mern
of House Gardener, King of the Reach, they

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:39.400
had the mightiest army in history, a so-called
iron fist to break the would-be conqueror.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:44.950
But while an iron fist can smash a man's face
in battle, you'd look silly hunting birds

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:50.170
or beasts with it, and Aegon had a creature
that was both.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:53.150
The kings had never even seen a dragon, let
alone fought one.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:57.990
They had fought each other for thousands of
years, and victory always went to the larger

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.350
army.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:03.810
Surely a force five times that of Aegon's
could manage one dragon.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:07.280
But Aegon arrived with three.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:11.530
Still, the Lannisters and Gardeners hoped
for victory.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:16.180
The battlefield they chose was a wide plain
with firm ground and clear skies.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.370
Perfect for archers and mounted cavalry.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:22.480
But neither of the kings spared a thought
for why the ground was firm.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:28.850
There had been no rain for a fortnight, which
meant all the wheat and grass on it were bone-dry.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.110
Perfect for dragons.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:33.620
At first, the kings looked like they would
emerge victorious.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:38.401
When the horn blew for battle, their armies
swept around Aegon's flanks, and their iron

00:03:38.401 --> 00:03:42.350
fist of mounted knights smashed through his
center before the dragons could even enter

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:43.390
the fray.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:49.130
But then Aegon and his sisters took flight
and unleashed their dragons, not on the soldiers,

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:52.070
but on the dry fields all around them.

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:57.930
The iron fist unclenched and became a hand
outstretched for mercy.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:01.740
As Aegon promised, he had none.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:06.870
More than four thousand men died in the fires,
another thousand escaping them.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:11.920
Tens of thousands returned home as monsters,
burned and scarred beyond recognition.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.290
House Gardener never returned at all.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:19.519
The Field of Fire, as the singers call it,
claimed the last of the Gardener line, and

00:04:19.519 --> 00:04:24.419
House Tyrell rose in their stead as Lords
of the Reach and Wardens of the South.

00:04:24.419 --> 00:04:29.569
As for my illustrious ancestor, when King
Loren saw the battle was lost, he rode through

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:31.340
a wall of flame and smoke to safety.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:38.259
Or at least to a heroic capture a day later,
where he lay his sword before Aegon and knelt.

00:04:38.259 --> 00:04:44.249
Aegon, true to his word, spared him and confirmed
House Lannister as Lords of Casterly Rock

00:04:44.249 --> 00:04:45.999
and Wardens of the West.

00:04:45.999 --> 00:04:46.999
Why wouldn't he?

00:04:46.999 --> 00:04:53.560
A Lannister always pays his debts, and now
we owed our lives to the crown.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.560
That was worth centuries of subservience,
at least.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:01.380
Besides, Aegon had a fetish for collecting
swords, not heads.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:06.520
He added Loren's to the pile his men had retrieved
from the Field of Fire and sent them back

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:07.520
to the Aegonfort.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:13.210
Petyr Baelish: Years later, the realm had
no sharper mind than Lord Tywin Lannister,

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:19.330
Hand to King Aerys II Targaryen, or as history
remembers him, "The Mad King."

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:25.400
He saw assassins and plots in every shadow,
heard whispers in silence, and burned men

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:30.729
alive, but his greatest madness by far was
driving away Lord Tywin.

00:05:30.729 --> 00:05:34.999
The Mad King then cycled through every mistake
of his ancestors.

00:05:34.999 --> 00:05:40.870
Soldiers, toadying lords and at the end, even
an alchemist, perhaps to save the crown's

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.740
growing expenses on wildfire.

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:46.999
Unfortunately, it didn't save his crown or
his dynasty.

00:05:46.999 --> 00:05:52.860
Tywin Lannister: As Aerys Targaryen's behavior
grew more and more erratic, the task of ruling

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:56.779
the Seven Kingdoms fell to me, Tywin Lannister.

00:05:56.779 --> 00:06:02.780
I had served Aerys for nearly twenty years
and as a result, the realm had prospered.

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:07.889
The royal coffers were full, the land was
at peace.

00:06:07.889 --> 00:06:15.550
But Aerys grew increasingly hostile, jealous
of the success many credited to me.

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:18.889
My power and influence unnerved him.

00:06:18.889 --> 00:06:24.479
The captain of my personal guard, Ser Ilyn
Payne, was once overheard making offhand comments

00:06:24.479 --> 00:06:28.770
regarding who was the true ruler of Westeros.

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:33.949
When the king was given this information,
he had llyn Payne's tongue ripped out with

00:06:33.949 --> 00:06:36.419
hot pincers.

00:06:36.419 --> 00:06:42.460
It was my desire to unite the Houses of Lannister
and Targaryen through marriage.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:47.650
My daughter, Cersei, would marry Aerys's eldest
son, Prince Rhaegar.

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:51.839
Such a union made perfect sense for all parties.

00:06:51.839 --> 00:06:57.900
However, Aerys's senses had begun to leave
him quite sometime earlier.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:03.710
Instead of uniting the royal family with its
most loyal and powerful ally, Aerys chose

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:11.050
instead to insult my family, indicating that
such a match was beneath Rhaegar.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:16.590
Instead, he chose Elia Martell of Dorne to
be Rhaegar's wife.

00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:24.660
As if to rub salt in my wounds, Aerys appointed
Jaime, my son, to the Kingsguard.

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:30.809
The Kingsguard may be an honor for lesser
families than ours, but it is a lifetime appointment

00:07:30.809 --> 00:07:35.900
that forces him to renounce all family holdings.

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:41.279
This creates a difficulty in naming an heir
to Casterly Rock.

00:07:41.279 --> 00:07:45.710
But Aerys knew all that.

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:49.309
I had grown tired of the king's constant provocation.

00:07:49.309 --> 00:07:57.330
Thus I resigned my post as Aerys's Hand and
returned to Casterly Rock with my considerable

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.900
forces.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:04.110
When Robert Baratheon rebelled against the
throne, Aerys grew fearful that I would join

00:08:04.110 --> 00:08:06.900
with Robert's forces and rise against him.

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:12.860
He thought himself clever and kept Jaime very
close as if warning me.

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:18.490
He sunk deeper and deeper into delusion, paranoia,
and violence.

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:25.479
Rhaegar Targaryen lay dead on the banks of
the Trident, his royal army shattered and

00:08:25.479 --> 00:08:27.449
in retreat.

00:08:27.449 --> 00:08:32.140
The days of the dragon kings were clearly
numbered.

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:36.600
Until that moment it would have been foolish
to commit Casterly Rock to either the crown

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:37.990
or the rebellion.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:45.020
What would House Lannister have to gain in
supporting a raving madman or in entering

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:49.660
a crusade to put Robert Baratheon on the Iron
Throne?

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:52.780
But chaos benefits no one.

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:58.330
It was time for House Lannister to do what
it could to ensure a return of peace and prosperity

00:08:58.330 --> 00:08:59.890
to the land.

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:06.400
I, Tywin Lannister, brought ten thousand Lannister
troops to the gates of King's Landing, in

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:11.330
order to bring the bloodshed to a quick and
decisive conclusion.

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:16.920
King Aerys had been sending ravens for months
begging for my support to end the uprising.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:21.550
In a way, his pleas had been answered.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:28.470
As I had suspected, Aerys opened the city
gates and welcomed my men.

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:34.500
Our plan was clear: crush Aerys's remaining
bannermen and remove the remnants of the royal

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:39.220
family as quickly and efficiently as possible.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:46.430
Any alternative meant years of further war
and a fragmented Seven Kingdoms.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:52.710
Our means were bloody, but the results speak
for themselves.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:59.080
As for Aerys, it is true he met his fate at
the hands of my son.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:04.380
Aerys had kept Jaime close during the rebellion,
thinking himself clever in keeping my son

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:10.090
as a hostage - should I decide to pledge support
to the rebel cause.

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:18.130
This proved to be his greatest mistake, for
when the time came Jaime did his duty as a

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:22.130
Lannister... and drove his sword into the
Mad King's back.

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:26.290
Jaime Lannister:My father's knights burst
into the hall in time to see the last of it,

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:30.860
so there was no way for me to vanish and let
some bragger steal the glory or blame.

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:35.190
I knew at once when I saw the way they looked
at me.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:37.060
It would be blame.

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:39.880
Lannister or no, I'd been one of Aerys' Kingsguard.

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:45.700
I commanded them to announce that the Mad
King was dead and to spare all those who yielded.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:48.560
They asked me if they should proclaim a new
king as well.

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:49.850
I knew what they meant.

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:55.150
Would it be my father, or Robert Baratheon,
or maybe the child Viserys who'd fled to Dragonstone?

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:58.790
A Targaryen boy king with my father as Hand
to rule in truth.

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:04.490
I thought of how Ned Stark and Robert Baratheon
would howl at this end to their great heroic

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:06.550
war, and I was tempted.

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:11.610
Then I glanced down again at Aerys, his life's
blood oozing from the wound and pooling on

00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:12.830
the floor around him.

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:16.770
"Proclaim who you bloody well like," I said.

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:22.240
I climbed the steps to the Iron Throne and
sat on it with my sword across my knees, waiting

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:22.610
to see who would come to claim the kingdom.

